# Framework (workspace)

**Role:** Core framework host (HTTP, sessions, middleware) and **examples**. Framework core stays UI-agnostic.

## Active UI stack

**Dependency direction (never reverse)**

`App / product` → `internal/ui` + `internal/views` → `github.com/fastygo/templ`

Reference implementation: `@Blank` (`github.com/fastygo/blank`) — `framework` + `templ` only. See `@Blank/go.mod`.

**Templ layering inside `github.com/fastygo/templ`**

| Layer | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Helpers | `utils/` | CVA (`Compose`), `Cn`, attrs, ARIA, `tags.go` |
| Primitives | `ui/` | button, input, form, layout, badge, … |
| Composites | `components/` | card, alert, breadcrumb, … |
| App shell | `internal/ui/` | layout, header, mobile sheet, toggles |
| Pages | `internal/views/` | view models and page bodies only |

Import shape in apps: `import "github.com/fastygo/templ/ui"` — do not deep-import `templ/ui/button` etc. in product code.

## Canceled — do not use for new work

- `github.com/fastygo/ui8kit` Go module
- `github.com/fastygo/elements`, `github.com/fastygo/blocks`
- Legacy `go-ui8kit/en` profile and UI8Kit-powered example patterns

Legacy Framework examples and docs may still mention UI8Kit — treat as historical archive, not the target stack.

## When changing UI

- **Reusable bricks** → `github.com/fastygo/templ` with matching `{name}.spec.md` (see `@Templ/.cursor/rules/templ-component-spec.mdc`).
- **App shell and chrome** → app `internal/ui/`; adapt patterns from `@Blank/internal/ui/layout/`.
- **Brand, tokens, campaign layout** → app CSS under `web/static/css/` — not in the templ registry.

## Styling

- Explicit Tailwind utility classes in `.templ` source; pass repo-root `.ui8px/` policy when present.
- Layout scope: 8px rhythm (`px-2`, `px-4`, `px-6`, `gap-4`). Control scope: finer 4px tuning (`px-3`, `py-1`, `h-7`) for compact primitives.
- Prefer semantic token classes (`bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`) over raw palette utilities.
- No `UtilityProps`, safelist generation, or hidden class indirection — Tailwind must see explicit classes or CSS `@apply`.

## Client behavior (not the UI8Kit Go module)

Dialog/sheet/mobile-menu behavior may use a committed `@ui8kit/aria` bundle in `web/static/js/ui8kit.js` plus `theme.js` for dark/light — see `@Blank`. This is a small static JS contract, not a `ui8kit` Go dependency.

## API shape

- Higher layers must not export lower-layer prop structs as their public contract.
- `Class string` and small part-class override structs are acceptable extension points.
- Compose `templ/ui` primitives in views; keep shell markup in `internal/ui/layout`.

**Examples:** New work follows `@Blank` + `templ`. Align with sibling repos' `.cursor/rules` and `ui8px` policies.
